/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  species/H2Tart.dat -- ONE model species, ONE typed file.

  The NEUTRAL, undissociated aqueous tartaric acid: the speciation MASTER of
  the tartrate family, from which HTart- and Tart2- are formed by the two
  dissociation records in chemistry/.  Its two conjugate bases were curated
  here on 2026-07-18 (species/HTart.dat, species/Tart.dat) but the master
  itself stayed behind in a case-local sidecar -- so the family had two homes
  and the neutral one was reachable from exactly one tutorial.  This record
  closes that: the family is now whole in the catalogue.

  Homonymy note (the `aq` suffix rule): the crystalline substance is the
  COMPONENT `tartaricAcid`, not `H2Tart`, so there is no name clash to
  disambiguate and the bare name stands.

  An `aqueousThermo { hfAq }` is deliberately ABSENT here.  The datum exists
  and is primary-cited -- Kochergina, Volkov, Krutov & Krutova, Russ. J. Phys.
  Chem. 80 (2006) 899-903, Table 5 gives Hf(H2Tart, sln, H2O, hypothetical
  nondissociated, 298.15 K) = -1295.9 kJ/mol, and it is already quoted in
  parameters/solution/tartaricAcid-water.dat -- but writing it HERE is a
  change of physics, not a change of address: the aqueous energy rung would
  start pricing the neutral master where today it does not.  This record was
  written as a MOVE and nothing else, so the value waits for a slice that
  measures what it does.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType modelSpecies;
schemaVersion 1;

name    H2Tart;
formula     "H2C4H4O6";
charge  0;
MW { value 150.087; unit g/mol;}
